        },
        {
          "type": "conjugation",
          "title": "vivir (-ir)",
          "note": "Drop -ir, keep viv-. Notice: -er and -ir are IDENTICAL except nosotros (-emos / -imos) and vosotros (-éis / -ís).",
          "verbIds": ["vivir"]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "The cheat code",
          "body": "Learn -ar and you're 80% of Spanish.\n\n-AR:  o, as, a, amos, áis, an\n-ER:  o, es, e, emos, éis, en\n-IR:  o, es, e, imos, ís, en\n\n-er and -ir share the first three and the last two. Only nosotros and vosotros differ. So a new -ir verb is nearly free once you know comer."
        }
      ],
